WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.745
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level A two.

2
00:00:06.045 --> 00:00:09.872
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:10.172 --> 00:00:17.109
Unit thirty-three: Adjective + Preposition. Today you will use the right preposition after adjectives.

4
00:00:17.409 --> 00:00:20.073
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:21.033 --> 00:00:24.289
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:25.150 --> 00:00:26.302
Interested in.

7
00:00:27.317 --> 00:00:30.291
Interested in means wanting to know more about something.

8
00:00:30.883 --> 00:00:32.778
I am interested in music.

9
00:00:33.383 --> 00:00:36.175
Your turn. Say: Interested in.

10
00:00:39.033 --> 00:00:40.255
Interested in.

11
00:00:41.017 --> 00:00:41.669
Good at.

12
00:00:42.683 --> 00:00:44.996
Good at means having skill in something.

13
00:00:45.583 --> 00:00:46.979
She is good at maths.

14
00:00:47.583 --> 00:00:50.421
Your turn. Say: Good at.

15
00:00:53.267 --> 00:00:54.001
Good at.

16
00:00:54.750 --> 00:00:55.716
Afraid of.

17
00:00:56.717 --> 00:00:59.250
Afraid of means feeling fear about something.

18
00:00:59.850 --> 00:01:01.490
He is afraid of dogs.

19
00:01:02.083 --> 00:01:04.469
Your turn. Say: Afraid of.

20
00:01:07.333 --> 00:01:08.195
Afraid of.

21
00:01:08.950 --> 00:01:10.009
Worried about.

22
00:01:11.017 --> 00:01:13.748
Worried about means feeling anxious about something.

23
00:01:14.350 --> 00:01:16.094
I am worried about the test.

24
00:01:16.683 --> 00:01:18.871
Your turn. Say: Worried about.

25
00:01:21.733 --> 00:01:22.990
Worried about.

26
00:01:23.750 --> 00:01:24.472
Proud of.

27
00:01:25.483 --> 00:01:28.655
Proud of means feeling happy about someone's success.

28
00:01:29.250 --> 00:01:30.530
I am proud of you.

29
00:01:31.117 --> 00:01:33.595
Your turn. Say: Proud of.

30
00:01:36.433 --> 00:01:37.283
Proud of.

31
00:01:38.050 --> 00:01:39.063
Different from.

32
00:01:40.050 --> 00:01:42.363
Different from means not the same as something.

33
00:01:42.950 --> 00:01:44.508
This is different from that.

34
00:01:45.117 --> 00:01:47.537
Your turn. Say: Different from.

35
00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:51.436
Different from.

36
00:01:52.183 --> 00:01:53.498
Excited about.

37
00:01:54.483 --> 00:01:58.352
Excited about means feeling happy and full of energy about something.

38
00:01:58.950 --> 00:02:00.613
We are excited about the trip.

39
00:02:01.217 --> 00:02:04.066
Your turn. Say: Excited about.

40
00:02:06.900 --> 00:02:08.157
Excited about.

41
00:02:08.917 --> 00:02:10.092
Angry with.

42
00:02:11.083 --> 00:02:13.733
Angry with means feeling cross about a person.

43
00:02:14.317 --> 00:02:15.771
She is angry with him.

44
00:02:16.383 --> 00:02:19.059
Your turn. Say: Angry with.

45
00:02:21.900 --> 00:02:22.994
Angry with.

46
00:02:23.800 --> 00:02:27.544
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:28.383 --> 00:02:32.324
Visal, are you interested in music? Notice the preposition.

48
00:02:33.417 --> 00:02:44.675
Yes, I am interested in music. Many adjectives are followed by a fixed preposition. We must learn the pairs: good at, afraid of, worried about, proud of.

49
00:02:45.783 --> 00:02:47.760
What comes after the preposition?

50
00:02:48.850 --> 00:02:59.472
A noun or a verb with -ing: She is good at maths. He is good at drawing. Not 'good at draw'. After a preposition, we always use the -ing form.

51
00:03:00.583 --> 00:03:02.014
How can I learn them?

52
00:03:03.117 --> 00:03:15.376
Learn the adjective with its preposition as one phrase. Make sentences about yourself: I am interested in science. I am proud of my school. Keep a list and review it often.

53
00:03:16.533 --> 00:03:17.976
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:18.817 --> 00:03:23.138
Grammar focus: Adjective plus preposition (+ noun and -ing).

55
00:03:23.438 --> 00:03:24.613
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:25.317 --> 00:03:27.154
I am interested in music.

57
00:03:28.050 --> 00:03:29.307
She is good at drawing.

58
00:03:30.217 --> 00:03:31.903
We are excited about the trip.

59
00:03:32.867 --> 00:03:42.694
Learn adjectives with their prepositions: interested in, good at, afraid of, worried about, proud of, excited about. After a preposition use a noun or the -ing form.

60
00:03:43.450 --> 00:03:46.961
Be careful! Don't say: He is good in drawing.

61
00:03:48.900 --> 00:03:50.969
Say: He is good at drawing.

62
00:03:51.269 --> 00:03:52.398
Say good at.

63
00:03:53.200 --> 00:03:55.678
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:56.467 --> 00:03:57.561
Fixed Pairs.

65
00:03:57.861 --> 00:04:01.160
I am interested in music, and my brother is good at drawing.

66
00:04:02.167 --> 00:04:05.397
She is afraid of dogs, but she is not worried about the exam.

67
00:04:06.400 --> 00:04:09.363
We are proud of our school and excited about the trip.

68
00:04:10.367 --> 00:04:12.378
His idea is different from mine.

69
00:04:13.367 --> 00:04:16.005
Our teacher was angry with the noisy students.

70
00:04:17.100 --> 00:04:21.171
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:22.017 --> 00:04:23.947
I am afraid blank spiders.

72
00:04:24.247 --> 00:04:26.878
A, of. B, at. C, from.

73
00:04:30.433 --> 00:04:32.061
The answer is A: of.

74
00:04:33.217 --> 00:04:34.763
She is good blank maths.

75
00:04:35.063 --> 00:04:38.113
A, in. B, at. C, on.

76
00:04:41.667 --> 00:04:43.330
The answer is B: at.

77
00:04:44.483 --> 00:04:46.286
We are excited blank the trip.

78
00:04:46.586 --> 00:04:49.287
A, about. B, of. C, with.

79
00:04:52.833 --> 00:04:54.543
The answer is A: about.

80
00:04:55.683 --> 00:04:57.393
Which sentence is correct?

81
00:04:57.693 --> 00:05:02.797
A, He is good at draw.. B, He is good at drawing.. C, He is good in drawing..

82
00:05:06.333 --> 00:05:09.215
The answer is B: He is good at drawing..

83
00:05:10.350 --> 00:05:13.069
According to the reading, who is good at drawing?

84
00:05:13.369 --> 00:05:17.139
A, my brother. B, my sister. C, the teacher.

85
00:05:20.700 --> 00:05:22.711
The answer is A: my brother.

86
00:05:23.900 --> 00:05:27.295
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:28.150 --> 00:05:30.927
Write a sentence with 'interested in' and one with 'good at'.

88
00:05:39.717 --> 00:05:41.263
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:41.563 --> 00:05:53.599
I am interested in science and I am good at maths. I use in after interested and at after good. After a preposition, I can use a noun or the -ing form of a verb.

90
00:05:53.899 --> 00:05:55.678
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:05:56.583 --> 00:06:01.778
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and adjective plus preposition (+ noun and -ing).

92
00:06:02.078 --> 00:06:06.611
Today's value is self-awareness. Know your strengths and keep growing.

93
00:06:06.911 --> 00:06:09.517
See you in Unit thirty-four. Goodbye!

94
00:06:09.817 --> 00:06:12.319
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

